  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>DOG STATION is a grooming salon at 4 rue de Trans in Draguignan. Its Facebook page presents it as grooming "for dogs of all breeds", and the Mappy directory lists bath, scissor cut, trimming and nail clipping for small and large dogs alike.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The salon can be reached on 09 81 06 21 99 or by email at dogstation@free.fr. Its Facebook page gives no opening hours; directories state 9am-7pm but disagree on the days: Tuesday to Saturday on Mappy, Monday to Saturday on Google Maps. A call before travelling will settle it. Published reviews are very positive: 100% recommend on Facebook (6 reviews), 5/5 from 4 reviews on Mappy and 4.6/5 from 63 reviews on Google Maps. The Mappy listing also mentions grooming without an appointment, to be confirmed with the salon.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: my human calls ahead to confirm the opening days and ask whether a slot is free without an appointment.</div>

      <h2>A salon rooted in its neighbourhood</h2>
      <p>In an article dated 24/03/2026, Nice-Matin explains that the salon is the drop-off point for the Draguignan Arts quarter's dragon contest, run by the quarter's neighbourhood association, which the salon's manager chairs. Entries could be dropped off until 22 June 2026.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The salon is on rue de Trans in Draguignan; the article places the contest in the shopping streets of the old centre, where entries are displayed in the Arts quarter's shops.</p>
